@joaom00  thx for your help, can confirm it has something to do with the minimal version of `dismissable-layer`, previously I was using the incompatible version.
since delete `node_modules` is not a direct approach for remote hosting.
At least for the version I was listing above, using the `overrides` with specific version is probably the way to go.
```ts
 "overrides": {
		"@radix-ui/react-dismissable-layer": "1.0.4"
	}
```
and don't use  `^` like `^1.0.4`, this will install multiple versions that it's above the the given versions as long as it satifisfies the constraints.

