### Steps to reproduce

Steps:

Set the `<Autocomplete>`'s width via the `sx` prop while also explicitly setting `fullWidth` to `false`.  

I tried using stackblitz as your documentation suggested, but that too is now bugged out for me. My will to recursively debug things just to report a bug is rapidly falling apart but I think this should illustrate the point here:

```typescript
import Autocomplete from '@mui/material/Autocomplete';
import TextField from '@mui/material/TextField';

export const App: FC<{ name: string }> = ({ name }) => {
  const opts = ['meep', 'beep', 'foo'];

  return (
    <div>
      <div style={{ width: '300px', border: '1px solid #0000FF' }}>
        {/* This should be full width inside the containing div */}
        <Autocomplete
          value="meep"
          options={opts}
          fullWidth={false}
          sx={{ width: '100%' }}
          size="small"
          placeholder="should be wide enough"
          renderInput={(params)=><TextField {...params}/>}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  );
};

```

### Current behavior

In 7.3.7, the above JSX would work to create a _de facto_ full-width autocomplete element (e.g., expanding `sx={{ width: "100%" }}` to fill a containing `<div>` block). In 7.3.8 now the Autocomplete is only as wide as needed to display the down-caret icon. 

See the attached screenshot to see several Autocomplete elements that used to be as wide as their containing column in the 2-column tables .

<img width="823" height="658" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a57502d-8cf5-446b-92ed-2df8d2f62497" />

I am pretty sure that pull request https://github.com/mui/material-ui/pull/47663 (which was switched from "breaking change" label to "non-breaking" at the last minute without much discussion) is the culprit. All of this worked fine last week on 7.3.7.


### Expected behavior

The autocomplete elements in the screenshot above should be as wide as the containing fixed-width column of the 2-column <table> layout they're in. This worked on 7.3.7.

### Context

This is a regression in 7.3.8. Ideally no code changes should be required.

