A workaround, for now, is to manually focus the input with no delay. Seems to work.

```typescript
  useEffect(() => {
    setTimeout(() => {
      if (inputRef.current) {
        inputRef.current.focus();
      }
    }, 0);
  }, []);
```

@RobinMalfait won't do an example, because the issue seems to be well described here https://github.com/tailwindlabs/headlessui/issues/390

It was about having a button with `autoFocus` prop in React, the initial transition wouldn't work then. So it has a workaround. 

Thank you for a quick response though.

candidates.issueBody:
It looks like something changed regarding the styles applied to `.euiComboBox__inputWrap`. In the [original PR adding fullWidth support](https://github.com/elastic/eui/commit/2312d6645b17857f55c4a15bd545e07680fd703d#diff-38d63a385c2b682be221f43841b4fb88) it looks like this enabled fullWidth:

```scss
 @include euiFormControlStyle($includeStates: false, $includeSizes: true);
```

Then in the [latest PR touching these styles](https://github.com/elastic/eui/commit/9e429dbdc343698acfa2ab44df038c279ee82d23#diff-38d63a385c2b682be221f43841b4fb88) we changed it to:

```scss
@include euiFormControlStyle($includeStates: false, $includeSizes: false);
@include euiFormControlSize(auto);
```

I haven't verified that this is the culprit but it looks possible.

CC @chandlerprall @cchaos
